{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1340674-my-obsession-with-gadgets-or-rather-a-particular-project","id":1340674,"title":"My Obsession With Gadgets (or rather, a particular project)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-10T13:51:19-07:00","id":1340674,"title":"My Obsession With Gadgets (or rather, a particular project)","content":"Hello. My name is Taidragon and I have an obsession with gadgets. No matter what character or game I am in as a Demon, making gadgets for clients will always be a thing (and probably never happen) as will a particular goal I've yet to make any headway on whatsoever.<br /> <br /> Namely, building a TARDIS-like conglomerate of lambdas.<br /> <br /> I say TARDIS-like because, having run an actual Doctor Who game and looking at the logistics of a Demon game, I don't want to throw time travel into a game beyond splinters or maybe Four Minutes Ago, or whatever time projects the Storyteller provides. What I want to build is a container that is bigger on the inside (a single room fitting in a closet sized box, about), has the ability to either make itself change shape or at least escape casual notice, and move from one place to another without having to take a mundane route. Naturally, this isn't something to be made without significant expenditure. At minimum this would require two lambdas and a single other gadget, possibly three lambdas overall, most of them retaining their individual effects as well as the combined effect - that's between 7-9 experiences without taking into account the cost of gaining the prerequisite powers, aether, the mundane hardware and the location for making such a thing safely.<br /> <br /> The problem I have with all this is that I wonder if I'm becoming too stuck on the idea of making this entirely out of Embeded lambdas, without any Exploits at all. I want to make this conglomerate so that if my character somehow gets separated from it, or has to put it into cold storage, or even just keeps it close at hand but can't use it, that it won't attract attention to itself via aetheric resonance and won't expire from a lack of maintenance/aether. This has had me scrub Exploits out of the design document bit by bit, even if they would make the project significantly easier to establish.<br /> <br /> I has gotten to the point I've started designing a second order lambda of Never Here, Alibi and Fulcrum Point to act as the &quot;engine&quot; to move the conglomerate around, a mile per success in an extended action (penalties for the distance possible) without being able to enter Infrastructure without triggering alarms (barring an exceptional success). It's here I'm wondering if I'm going a step too far to try and make this goal feasible.<br /> <br /> I suppose my question after all that is this: am I letting this goal hang over me too much? Should I just set it aside and let it rest? Am I focusing way too much on the quiet aspect and just let exploits be a part of this, for better or worse?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-10T14:07:39-07:00","id":1340678,"title":"","content":"One thing that discernably make this hard is that the concept <i>seems</i> like it's doable from the gadget direction, but is suitably complex enough that it feasibly is Suborned Infrastructure territory. Consider that as you will.<br /> <br /> If I were to do this, the powers I'd go with would be Quick Change for the change shape aspect, Two Places at Once for both the travel and the interior, and maybe Rip The Gates for good measure.<br /> <br /> BUT if you REALLY want how I'd do it, I would actually start with the Bolthole Merit (since the bigger on the inside, multiple exit, and camouflage are all covered by that) and support that with gadget functions depending on the flavors to the idea you want to present.<br /> <br /> Actually, Embedded/Exploited/Lambda Boltholes sound like a cool idea in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-10T14:56:46-07:00","id":1340686,"title":"","content":"One of the earlier attempts I had at this concept actually did use a Bolthole and a Two Places At Once gadget inside to move it around, but that was meant to be a sort of starter before I moved onto my big goal at the time: find a Lare, bond with it and augment it with gadgets to allow it to travel around safely. I even had my Demon Fall because they were an Analyst who surveyed the city, and accidentally locked on to a Lare who was suffering. The idea that an Angel of the God-Machine could be left to suffer like that is what made my character disconnect. Unfortunately, the Storyteller didn't understand what a Lare was and so never included any without telling me in the year the game went through, and I get the feeling that (and how long it took for me to actually have the opportunity to get <i>that</i> far) has impacted my desire to use Boltholes after that.<br /> <br /> Still, a Bolthole is, if nothing else, a good shortcut for the shell and or the bigger on the inside aspect. I initially considered Exploiting the entrance of one with Rip The Gates (and then Two Places At Once) at a very early incarnation of the idea, but someone else pointed out that there was no real way for me to access it from the inside like that, and so it just kind of fell apart there.<br /> <br /> As for the idea of making this Suborned Infrastructure, I did briefly consider it, and one ST did try to give me an Infrastructure to work with that was bigger on the inside (but made it the hub of a ton of Infrastructure and Angel activity that would take a massive amount of time and effort to suborn, again, <i>without telling us</i> but that's another topic), but it doesn't really appeal to me. I like this being something unique to my character, something I can claim was my ideas, my work, my efforts. Stealing it from the God-Machine just kind of... robs that feeling, and means that It explicitly knows what I've done and how It can find me. This might be something I need to kind of get over.<br /> <br /> I've got my ideas below, but it is a bit of a ramble so I'm spoilering it for the interests of keeping this post not being a whole page by default.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">My current plans with the shell was to make a sort of box out of high definition screens with both Synthesis and Alibi installed - Synthesis allows it to scan its surroundings (allowing the side benefit of allowing whoever is inside to get a read of the outside via connected device), Alibi lets it change shape to fit in with its surroundings. Their combined effect is that if the object appears to match their surroundings people acknowledge it but it's just sort of <i>there</i>, a background detail. Yes, there's a cabinet in the corner that wasn't there before, but it's just a cabinet, move on. No, I don't know why we have a second fridge in the staff kitchen, but it's a fridge, move on. However, a drawback to this is that if someone has a reason to investigate the shell, or they know what it really is, they bypass this power.<br /> <br /> The Alibi and combined aspects are ones I've swapped a couple of times, changing out the Embed so that it either is ignored if it matches its surroundings and the combined effect allows it to change shape, or whatever. The hardware itself has been troublesome since I've wanted to custom make that, but my route so far has been to make <i>another</i> Lambda out of a 3d printer, and that... well, it has had its own foibles.<br /> <br /> The Bigger On The Inside aspect is one that has actually been pretty stable since inception - In My Pocket to make a sealed space without windows to be larger inside than out without affecting the exterior dimensions. So long as it could fit through a doorway that can be sealed, it can remain inside the space without compromising it, but the room has its limits and it is still orientated with the exterior. The exact hardware has eluded me (I've been thinking of either a disco ball or an infinity mirror), and I've wanted to lambda it to make it both more durable and have more benefits, but that has been something I've waffled on a lot.<br /> <br /> The engine... has been a lot less defined. It's the only one I've kept Exploits in, but <i>what</i> Exploits I've not been able to decide on. Two Places At Once, Behind The Curtain, Decoy, Four Minutes Ago, Living Shadow and even Solitary Confinement have all been bandied around and I've not been able to really settle on it. It also doesn't help that getting the Exploits for this project without making it difficult to use them was a difficult choice in and of itself. It was always going to be a lambda, have the condition it was in a room that was bigger inside than outside to function as a way to broaden the scale it would operate on and has kept the idea that it moved based on a success-per-mile for an extended action, but aside from that it's been a mess. The Never Here/Alibi/Fulcrum Point idea was born both from being able to get the Embeds easier for more practical means, but also for the idea of it being harder to notice and not going to die just because someone snuck in somehow and stole all its aether a week ago and I didn't notice because we've been so extremely busy I couldn't check (the business is more common than you'd think in my Demon games).</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Also, thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> for the feedback, it is appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 10-11-2019, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}